#. type: Title-text
#: ../scene.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Follow with variables"
msgstr "Percorso con variabili"

#. type: Resume-text
#: ../scene.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use variables in order to store the parameters of the path."
msgstr "Usa variabili per conservare i parametri del percorso."

#. type: ScriptName-text
#: ../scene.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "Move"
msgstr "Move"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../help/help.E.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Exercise"
msgstr "Esercizio"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This exercise is very similar to the previous one. The bot must move exactly in the same way, but when writing the program, you must use a new concept that is extremely important in programming: <a cbot|var>variables</a>.\n"
"We saw that all the pads are at a distance form each other of 20 meters. And all the rotations performed consist in 90 degree angles. Instead of rewriting the same values over and over again in the program, we can store them in a variable: "
msgstr ""
"Il percorso è identico al precedente, ma questa volta devi usare un concetto fondamentale: le <a cbot|var>variabili</a>.\n"
"Tutte le piattaforme distano 20 m e tutte le curve sono di 90 gradi. Invece di ripetere gli stessi valori, conservali in variabili: "

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Instead of:\n"
"<c/><s/>\tmove(20);"
msgstr ""
"Invece di:\n"
"<c/><s/>\tmove(20);"

#. type: Source code
#: ../help/help.E.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tturn(90);\n"
"\tmove(20);\n"
"\tturn(-90);\n"
"\t..."
msgstr ""
"\tturn(90);\n"
"\tmove(20);\n"
"\tturn(-90);\n"
"\t..."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:12
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We write :\n"
"<c/><s/>\tdist = 20;"
msgstr ""
"Scrivi:\n"
"<c/><s/>\tdist = 20;"

#. type: Source code
#: ../help/help.E.txt:14
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tdir = 90;\n"
"\tmove(dist);\n"
"\tturn(dir);\n"
"\tmove(dist);\n"
"\tturn(-dir);\n"
"\t..."
msgstr ""
"\tdir = 90;\n"
"\tmove(dist);\n"
"\tturn(dir);\n"
"\tmove(dist);\n"
"\tturn(-dir);\n"
"\t..."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../help/help.E.txt:21
#, no-wrap
msgid "Variables"
msgstr "Variabili"

#. type: Bullet: '1)'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:23
#, no-wrap
msgid "The name,"
msgstr "Il nome,"

#. type: Bullet: '2)'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "The type of the content,"
msgstr "Il tipo del contenuto,"

#. type: Bullet: '3)'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:25
#, no-wrap
msgid "The content."
msgstr "Il contenuto."

#. type: \t; header
#: ../help/help.E.txt:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "The name"
msgstr "Il nome"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:28
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use the name to refer to a variable. For example, instead of writing "
"<c/>move(20);<n/>, write <c/>move(dist);<n/>: \"dist\" is the name of the "
"variable. You can choose almost any name for a variable, for example "
"<code>dist</code>, <code>dir</code>, <code>p2</code>, <code>a</code>, "
"<code>x</code>, <code>nothing_2_grab</code>, etc."
msgstr ""
"Usa il nome per riferirti alla variabile: invece di <c/>move(20);<n/> scrivi"
" <c/>move(dist);<n/>, dove «dist» è il nome. Puoi scegliere quasi "
"liberamente: <code>dist</code>, <code>dir</code>, <code>p2</code>, "
"<code>a</code>, <code>x</code>, <code>nothing_2_grab</code> e così via."

#. type: \t; header
#: ../help/help.E.txt:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "The type"
msgstr "Il tipo"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:32
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code><a cbot|int>int</a></code> for a whole number (12, -500, etc.)"
msgstr "<code><a cbot|int>int</a></code> per un intero (12, -500, ecc.)"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:33
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code><a cbot|float>float</a></code> for a real number (3.14, 0.2, -99.98, "
"etc.)"
msgstr ""
"<code><a cbot|float>float</a></code> per un reale (3.14, 0.2, -99.98, ecc.)"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:34
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code><a cbot|string>string</a></code> for a character string (\"Hello!\", "
"\"Nothing to grab\", etc.)"
msgstr ""
"<code><a cbot|string>string</a></code> per testi («Ciao!», «Niente da "
"prendere», ecc.)"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:35
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code><a cbot|point>point</a></code> for the x,y,z-coordinates of a point in"
" space"
msgstr ""
"<code><a cbot|point>point</a></code> per coordinate x,y,z di un punto nello "
"spazio"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:36
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code><a cbot|object>object</a></code> for the information about an object "
"(bot, building, etc.) "
msgstr ""
"<code><a cbot|object>object</a></code> per informazioni su un oggetto "
"(robot, edificio, ecc.) "

#. type: \t; header
#: ../help/help.E.txt:38
#, no-wrap
msgid "The content"
msgstr "Il contenuto"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:39
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The content of a variable can be a number, a string, coordinates, etc., "
"according to the type of the variable. The content of a variable can change "
"many times during the execution of a program. "
msgstr ""
"Il contenuto può essere un numero, una stringa, coordinate o altro, secondo "
"il tipo, e può cambiare molte volte durante il programma. "

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:41
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before you can use a variable, you have to declare it. For example, before "
"you can use the two variables <code>dist</code> and <code>dir</code>, you "
"must declare them with the following lines: "
msgstr ""
"Prima di usare una variabile devi dichiararla. Per esempio, per "
"<code>dist</code> e <code>dir</code> scrivi: "

#. type: Source code
#: ../help/help.E.txt:43
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tfloat  dist;\n"
"\tfloat  dir;"
msgstr ""
"\tfloat  dist;\n"
"\tfloat  dir;"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:46
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now you can use the two variables. To put the value 20 into "
"<code>dist</code> and 90 into <code>dir</code>, write:"
msgstr "Ora assegna 20 a <code>dist</code> e 90 a <code>dir</code>:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../help/help.E.txt:48
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tdist = 20;\n"
"\tdir = 90;"
msgstr ""
"\tdist = 20;\n"
"\tdir = 90;"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:51
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now you can move and turn the bot with the instructions <code><a "
"cbot|move>move</a></code> and <code><a cbot|turn>turn</code></a>:"
msgstr ""
"Puoi poi muovere e ruotare il robot con <code><a cbot|move>move</a></code> e"
" <code><a cbot|turn>turn</code></a>:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../help/help.E.txt:53
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tmove(dist);\n"
"\tturn(dir);"
msgstr ""
"\tmove(dist);\n"
"\tturn(dir);"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:56
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can also use a whole <a cbot|expr>mathematical expression</a> instead of"
" just the variable:"
msgstr "Puoi usare anche un’intera <a cbot|expr>espressione matematica</a>:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../help/help.E.txt:58
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tmove(dist+100);\n"
"\tturn(-dir);"
msgstr ""
"\tmove(dist+100);\n"
"\tturn(-dir);"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:61
#, no-wrap
msgid "The latter instruction will be needed to turn the bot right. "
msgstr "Quest’ultima istruzione serve per girare a destra. "

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:63
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, rewrite the program of the previous exercise, but use a variable for "
"the distance and another variable for the angle of the rotation. "
msgstr ""
"Riscrivi il programma precedente usando una variabile per la distanza e una "
"per l’angolo. "

#. type: \t; header
#: ../help/help.E.txt:65
#, no-wrap
msgid "See also"
msgstr "Vedi anche"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:66
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<a cbot>Programming</a>, <a cbot|type>types</a> and <a "
"cbot|category>categories</a>."
msgstr ""
"<a cbot>Programmazione</a>, <a cbot|type>tipi</a> e <a "
"cbot|category>categorie</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "A <a cbot|var>variable</a> is composed of three elements: "
msgstr "Una <a cbot|var>variabile</a> comprende tre elementi: "

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:31
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The type of a variable determines what kind of information the variable can "
"contain. According to the type, a variable can contain a whole number, a "
"real number, a character string, the coordinates of a point, etc. Here is a "
"list with the most common variable types: "
msgstr ""
"Il tipo determina le informazioni ammesse: interi, reali, testi, coordinate "
"e così via. Ecco i tipi più comuni: "
